    "description": "PROENERGY manufactures, services, and operates aeroderivative power generation equipment and related contracted generation assets for utilities, municipalities, data centers, and industrial customers. Its business spans turbine and package manufacturing, turnkey project execution, contracted power, and lifecycle maintenance, which gives the company exposure to both equipment and operating infrastructure cash flows. The operating model is asset-heavy and service-intensive, with revenue supported by long-lived power assets, maintenance contracts, and engineered equipment delivery. Public disclosures tie the platform to headquarters and manufacturing operations in Sedalia, Missouri and to the WattBridge portfolio of approximately 2.4 gigawatts of contracted gas peaking capacity in ERCOT. ECP acquired a majority stake in 2024, positioning the company around fast-start generation, aero services, and flexible power solutions.",
